## Dotfiles — cross-agent mirrors

**Generated config.** `.claude/rules/*.md`, `.claude/CLAUDE.md` and `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md` are generated by `claude-gen` (`.claude/gen`, ADR-0001) from `.claude/src/`: edit `.claude/src/rules/<name>.md.tmpl`, `.claude/src/skills/<name>.{yaml,md.tmpl}` (frontmatter in the YAML, body in the template), or `rules.yaml`, `models.yaml`, `gen.yaml`, then run `go -C .claude/gen run . --root "$PWD"`. A generated file carries `Code generated by claude-gen; DO NOT EDIT.` in its first lines; `just lint` fails when one differs from a fresh render (`--check`). The `guard-generated.sh` PreToolUse hook asks before an Edit/Write on any file marked `Code generated … DO NOT EDIT`, in every project.

`dotfiles/.claude/` is the source of truth. The tool-neutral mirrors are generated too: `cursor/rules/*.mdc` from `.claude/src/mirrors/cursor/<name>.mdc.tmpl` (condensed by hand; a catalog rule enters as `{{"{{"}}summary "<id>"{{"}}"}}`, so a rule listing a `cursor/<name>` target needs a `summary`), `kilocode/rules/*.md` from the same templates without frontmatter, and `codex/AGENTS.md` from `.claude/src/agents.md.tmpl`, which composes the Cursor bodies. After changing a mirrored source, update its Cursor template and regenerate. (Not `/sync-docs`, which syncs a project's docs with its code.)

Which source each Cursor template condenses:

| Cursor mirror | Source |
|---|---|
| `global-standards` | `CLAUDE.md` (+ the test-double summary) |
| `testing` | `rules/testing.md` + `rules/testing-authoring.md` |
| `verification` | `rules/verification.md` (+ the live-target probe from `rules/browser-automation.md`) |
| `development-practices` | `rules/development-practices.md` (+ the debugging method from `skills/fix/SKILL.md`) |
| `code-review-reception` / `documentation-sync` | the same-named rule |
| `go` / `python` / `typescript-react` | `rules/standards-golang.md` / `standards-python.md` / `standards-typescript.md` + `standards-frontend.md` |

Not mirrored: `task-and-workflow`, `communication`, `mcp-servers`, `linear`, `browser-automation`, `standards-backend`, `dotfiles-sync`, and all skills/agents.

**Skill evals.** A skill's evals live in `.claude/skills/<name>/evals/` (claude-gen leaves that directory alone): `trigger-eval.json` holds the skill-creator trigger queries, and each `<case>/` (a `case.yaml` or `prompt.md`, a `fixture.sh` scaffold, `graders/*.md`) is a `claude plugin eval` behavior case. A change to a skill's procedure runs its cases with `just eval <name>` (paid; `--runs 1 --ablation none` while iterating); a new skill or a fixed misbehavior gets a case.
